WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.830
A roast is the hardest
thing to do in comedy.

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:04.580
I compare it to our Olympics.

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:07.880
I really feel like there's
nothing else to compare it to.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:09.940
You have to go, as soon
as I asked to do the roast

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:11.180
I start writing jokes,
and then you have to

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:12.260
start taking those jokes out

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.270
and then I have to go from club to club

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:16.460
and just tell the people watching,

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.370
I'm like, imagine Rob Lowe is here,

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:19.500
just for the sake of things.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.860
I'm about to say a lot
of mean things about him.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:23.700
Picture him here laughing,

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.200
and then you get laughs, but it's like

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.350
you can't ever really know
how it's gonna do in the room.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:29.960
There's no way to tell.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.660
And so, it's so much preparation

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:33.640
and then you finally do it

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:37.300
and luckily it's always a great crowd

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.810
and they're ready for
it and it's gone well,

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:40.960
but the first time doing
it, I was terrified

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:44.730
and I always for the past three roasts,

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:46.210
the three that I've done,

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:48.800
I always get a point of
utter exhaustion beforehand

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:51.710
because I've trained so hard

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:54.950
and that night it just feels
so good doing it and being done

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.350
because you just never know.

00:00:57.219 --> 00:00:58.460
It's one of the only things in comedy

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:00.260
that you can't really prepare for

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.860
because it's such a unique performance.

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:05.070
I'm kind of not surprised,

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:07.420
but it's interesting
to hear that you test,

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:09.410
or have the ability to
go test the jokes out,

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:11.100
which makes perfect sense.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:11.933
Why wouldn't you?

00:01:11.933 --> 00:01:12.910
You're in front of the mic

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:14.350
and you're doing your thing anyway,

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:18.020
because for me, I'm not
a professional at it,

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:21.180
I had never tested one of
those jokes that I got.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.700
So I'm literally, this is the
first time I'm telling it,

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:25.110
the first time anybody's hearing.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:26.810
I have no idea if people are gonna think

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:28.780
it's too mean, not mean enough, whatever,

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:31.180
and it's all live and it's
in front of everybody.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:32.013
I know!

00:01:32.013 --> 00:01:35.020
I always worry about the
stars during these roasts

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:37.400
because as a comedian, Jeff Ross, me,

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:39.620
and usually the other couple comics,

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:42.037
we're all at the clubs all
night doing our roast sets,

00:01:42.037 --> 00:01:43.760
and then we think about the actors

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:46.290
that are on the dais,

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:48.390
and I'm like, they're just gonna wing it.

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:50.610
But the thing is, they always kill!

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.040
You guys always do well.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:53.720
You have one rehearsal,

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:56.340
but you're professionals

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:59.240
so you always do well,

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:01.210
but it is funny that I feel the need

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:04.400
to go out and run the set like 60 times.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:05.690
That's crazy!

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:09.280
Like honestly Rob, every
single time I do a roast

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:12.557
I am so run down because I'm
doing like five sets a night,

00:02:12.557 --> 00:02:14.510
having all these sheets of paper,

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:17.040
scratching out jokes, rewriting
them, reorganizing them.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:19.550
I hired a writer's assistant last year.

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:21.260
I hired writers.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:23.060
I had a writers' room last year.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:24.635
I'm not even joking.

00:02:24.635 --> 00:02:25.549
What?

00:02:25.549 --> 00:02:26.536
It was nuts.

00:02:26.536 --> 00:02:27.770
I lost money on it, no joke.

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:31.420
But it is the biggest opportunity

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:34.410
for a comedian to make a
splash and to really be seen.

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:36.660
It's like we don't have
The Tonight Show anymore

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:37.493
with Johnny Carson.

00:02:37.493 --> 00:02:40.210
We don't have the same.

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:44.970
It's just the best platform
for a comedian to make it,

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:47.310
so I work my tail off on it

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:49.620
and every year I tell my friends,

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:51.470
remind me never to do one of these again

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:54.610
because I'm losing my mind
and I hate this process,

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:55.560
and then I do it and I'm like,

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:57.600
oh my god, that was the
best night of my life.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.350
I feel like they're pregnancies.

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:01.590
I'm always like, I don't
want to do this again!

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:02.490
And then I'm holding my baby

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.950
and I'm like, I love it,
I want to have another.

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:05.981
Yeah.

00:03:05.981 --> 00:03:07.773
I mean, I don't have kids,
but I compare it to that.

